# DXMT's headless programs for the 4b-2 gate (gate.sh): name|exe|arguments|prefixes. The arguments are those of
# dxmt/check.sh's first `run ours` line for the program; @T is the tests folder (dxmt/tests, or its copy in the VM
# share), @S its shaders and @X the programs' own folder (the share's dxmt-tests), which each side passes as Z: paths.
# The d3d12_xess rows are check.sh's: XeSS answered by MetalFX through Wine's builtin libxess.dll, which the program
# loads by full path from a copy of itself (@X/xess/libxess.dll); libxess=b on both sides makes that the builtin.
# The d3d12_dlss rows too: DLSS answered by MetalFX through DXMT's signed nvngx.dll in system32, loaded by full path as
# the NGX SDK does; their runs have MACNEUTRON_DLSS=1 on macOS and DXMT_ENABLE_NVEXT=1 in the guest (ref.sh, dxmt.sh).
# Not d3d12_xess's cycles case: its line holds GPU memory sizes, a few MB apart in the guest (its buffers are blob memory,
# freed when the guest drains its frees); its own limits pass on both sides. A line of output is compared when it starts with one
# of the program's prefixes (its own printf lines; Wine's, DXMT's and the launcher's never count). The d3d11 and d3d10 rows
# (Direct3D forwarding M4) take their shaders as DXBC from @S, which dxbc.exe compiled on the macOS runtime.
